R('b2-q83','c','job-queue','Queueing; Maximum concurrent runs',
 'A job’s maximum concurrent runs and queueing policy determine how overlapping triggers are queued or skipped. Task timeouts and warehouse permissions address different execution stages.',
 'A skipped concurrency-limited run points first to job admission settings.',
 'Warehouse permissions can prevent a SQL task from executing, but they do not explain a job admission message explicitly tied to concurrency/queueing. The failure category is different.',
 'A task timeout acts after a task is running too long. It is not the job-level policy that skips an overlapping triggered run.',
 'Check max_concurrent_runs and whether queueing is enabled. These govern the observed overlapping-run admission behavior.',
 'Spot instance shortages affect provisioning/reliability after compute is requested. They are not the direct configuration named by a job concurrency queue message.')
R('b2-q84','c','bundle-settings,bundles','targets; Workspace settings',
 'Per-environment targets can override workspace host and root_path in bundle configuration. Source pipeline logic should not need environment-specific edits merely to deploy to a different workspace.',
 'Version deployment settings alongside source, then select the intended target explicitly.',
 'Environment variables can provide some inputs, but a global local-machine variable is not the project’s declarative per-target workspace definition. It also makes environment selection less reviewable.',
 'Hard-coding workspace deployment settings in Python mixes infrastructure configuration with pipeline logic. It prevents the clean target-based separation requested.',
 'The targets section supports environment-specific workspace overrides in databricks.yml. This is the appropriate location for host and workspace deployment paths.',
 'README text documents a configuration but is not parsed as bundle deployment settings. Writing a host there does not select the deployment workspace.')
R('b2-q85',None,'jobs,job-if-else','Run if condition options; If/else task',
 'A task has one run-if policy over its dependency set, not independently assigned Success/Failure policies per edge as these options suggest. Implement the required mixed condition with explicit supported control flow and observable state, not an invented negative-dependency widget.',
 'All done, all succeeded, and at least one failed aggregate dependency outcomes; none alone means A succeeded AND B failed.',
 'All done waits for completion regardless of outcome and the printed condition widget is not a documented setting here. It does not establish the required mixed success/failure predicate.',
 'A negative dependency is not the documented dependency configuration. Success on one edge plus a fabricated negative edge does not implement this DAG.',
 'Two dependency chains do not give one task two different per-edge run-if policies. The source C answer assumes an unsupported configuration model.',
 'Task values contain values explicitly published by tasks, not automatically every task’s result state. A failed producer may never publish one, so the sequence is not a verified complete implementation as written.',status='unsupported-dependency-model')
R('b2-q86','d','compute,single-node','Jobs compute; Autoscaling',
 'A scheduled jobs cluster provides job-scoped lifecycle and configurable autoscaling for predictable batch ETL. The serverless option here is specifically a SQL warehouse, not generic serverless jobs compute.',
 'Do not treat SQL warehouses and serverless notebook/jobs compute as interchangeable.',
 'All-purpose compute supports interactive execution but may stay running outside the job. It is not the most direct job-scoped lifecycle offered.',
 'A serverless SQL warehouse is appropriate for warehouse-supported SQL tasks. The question does not state that these general ETL pipelines are restricted to SQL warehouse execution.',
 'A fixed single-node cluster cannot provide the requested automatic distributed scaling. It may also lack resources for the stated large-volume transformations.',
 'A scheduled job compute cluster can scale under its configuration and terminate after the job. That matches periodic batch work and avoiding idle compute between executions.')
R('b2-q87','a','job-if-else','Configure an If/else task; Task values',
 'An If/else task compares the published record_count task value with 1000000 and routes downstream tasks on its true/false result. Run-if status policies do not inspect the numeric count.',
 'Branch on a business metric with If/else; branch on success/failure with run-if policies.',
 'A reads the task value in the condition operand and compares it to the threshold. The true and false branches can select high-volume versus normal processing.',
 'For each repeats a nested task over an array, not a numeric threshold branch. A scalar record count is not an iteration plan.',
 'Retries repeat work after failure and do not implement a normal business branch. Repeating until volume changes is not the required deterministic workflow.',
 'Run-if conditions inspect dependency result status rather than the numeric record_count. Both upstream runs could succeed with different counts, so status alone is insufficient.')
